  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "For $\\triangle ABC$ we are given that $\\angle A=45^{\\circ}$, $a=\\sqrt{5}$ and $c=3$. Find $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$b=\\sqrt{2}$ or $2\\sqrt{2}$.",
      "worked": "Using the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2&=b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos A\\\\5&=b^2+3^2-2(b)(3)\\cos45^{\\circ}\\\\5&=b^2+9-6b\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\0&=b^2-3\\sqrt{2}b+4\\\\0&=(b-\\sqrt{2})(b-2\\sqrt{2})\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $b=\\sqrt{2}$ or $b=2\\sqrt{2}$. Both values give valid triangles.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
